<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output up 5.2 pct in September.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output up 5.2 pct in September.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (unadjusted) rose 5.2 percent in September after a 0.8 percent rise in August, and was 8.0 percent higher than in September 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Industrial output rose 8.8 percent in the January-September period, against a 10.8 percent rise in the same period of 1995.  </p>
<p>POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	SEPTEMBER   AUGUST     SEPT 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	  5.2     0.8  (0.7)     1.6</p>
<p> yr/yr change			  8.0     7.0  (6.9)     7.3</p>
<p> index (mthly avg 1994=100)     23.7     n/a (20.6)   *36.1</p>
<p> mining m/m change		   5.9    -1.0 (-1.6)    -2.2</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		-0.2    -7.9 (-8.5)    -4.6</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	  4.3     0.8  (0.7)     1.2</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	9.2     9.4  (9.3)     8.9</p>
<p> utilities m/m change	     14.7     3.0  (3.0)     9.5</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	    4.2    -0.2 (-0.1)     1.6</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>NOTES: Revised data in brackets. September 1996 had 22 working days, while August 1996 and September 1995 had 23 working days. (*) 1992=100</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
